/2026/10/16/citizens-cfg-q3-2026-earnings-call-transcript/","lens":{"theater":[0,0,0,0.0],"cinema":[0,0,0,0.0],"imax":[0,0,0,0.0],"streaming":[0,0,0,0.0],"dtc":[0,0,0,0.0],"ai_spend":[0,0,0,0.0],"tariffs":[0,0,0,0.0],"pricing_power":[0,0,0,0.0],"cost_cuts":[0,0,0,0.0],"guidance":[0,0,0,0.0,{"raise":0,"reaffirm":0,"cut":0}],"ai_disruption":[0,0,0,0.0]},"move":{"r1":-0.0011,"r5":0.0285,"r20":0.0225,"r1_spy":0.01,"r5_spy":0.0387,"r20_spy":0.0416,"r1_sector":-0.0056,"r5_sector":0.0036,"r20_sector":-0.0306,"etf":"XLF"}}],"quotes":[{"c":"CFG 2016 Q2","e":"cfg","d":"2016-07-22","l":"pricing_power","r":"management","s":"Eric Aboaf","x":"One of the natural ways to do that is to take price up, you've got to do that carefully.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2016 Q2","e":"cfg","d":"2016-07-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bruce Van Saun","x":"We expect a gain of approximately $70 million, a portion of which will be utilized to cover restructuring costs associated with TOP III.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2016 Q2","e":"cfg","d":"2016-07-22","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Eric Aboaf","x":"Up 5% sequentially and $0.11 year-over-year, those second quarter 2015 results included $40 million of restructuring charges and special expense items.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2016 Q3","e":"cfg","d":"2016-10-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Eric Aboaf","x":"And lastly, we incurred a $17 million expense associated with our TOP III expense initiatives related to severance and consultants.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2016 Q3","e":"cfg","d":"2016-10-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Eric Aboaf","x":"In addition, once we do that preparatory work, we need to take severance and reserve effectively for the anticipated head count actions.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2017 Q2","e":"cfg","d":"2017-07-21","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"On the revenue side, we are focused on building new channels primarily to enhancing our digital capabilities and building out our direct to consumer mortgage program and leveraging our call centre to offer solutions to our customers.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2017 Q2","e":"cfg","d":"2017-07-21","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"We'll optimize our technology infrastructure and streamline our network support.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2017 Q3","e":"cfg","d":"2017-10-20","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"In addition, we are investing in a direct to consumer origination platform which we believe will provide a lower cost challenge to originate performing mortgages.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2017 Q3","e":"cfg","d":"2017-10-20","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Bruce Van Saun","x":"But we still have to, I think hone the model to get more conforming loan officers that are better integrated into the branches and build some additional capabilities direct to consumer potentially enter into the correspondent business.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2017 Q3","e":"cfg","d":"2017-10-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Ken Zerbe","x":"Are you done with most of sort of the restructuring of the deposit side, such that we are at a good point between wholesale borrowings and core deposits, or is there more to go?","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2017 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2018-01-19","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Bruce Van Saun","x":"Let's move and invest in our direct to consumer business and then let's get scale in the servicing by buying some MSRs.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2017 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2018-01-19","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Don McCree","x":"You talked about the shift to direct to consumer.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2017 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2018-01-19","l":"dtc","r":"management","s":"Don McCree","x":"But as we've been doing that, we’ve been making 1 billion investment in building the capability for direct to consumer, so building the data now really need to underpin your ability to do direct mail and digital offering and that investment has been made.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2017 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2018-01-19","l":"dtc","r":"analyst","s":"Ellen Taylor","x":"And so I was just going to add one thing that our direct to consumer marketing effort in home equity has been really successful following the build out in data and analytics and we improved our originations in that channel from about 150 million in 2015 to over 1 billion in 2017.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2018 Q1","e":"cfg","d":"2018-04-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"We continue to remain disciplined on the expense front as we identify opportunities to streamline our operations and organization to find efficiencies.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2018 Q1","e":"cfg","d":"2018-04-20","l":"cost_cuts","r":"analyst","s":"Bruce Van Saun","x":"We continue to find new ways to streamline our processes and organization in order to become more efficient and to self-fund these investments.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2018 Q2","e":"cfg","d":"2018-07-20","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"We expect to raise about $2 billion of deposits through this nationwide direct to consumer digital channel by the end of the year.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2018 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2019-01-18","l":"streaming","r":"management","s":"Brad Conner","x":"We keep talking about the investments we've made in data and analytics capability but that really does allow us to grow our direct-to-consumer side of business.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2018 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2019-01-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Bruce Van Saun","x":"We've made, I think, the right investments to get the right size of sales force in place, the right approach to selling, the right product capability.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2018 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2019-01-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Donald McCree","x":"And we've also built a restructuring business, which is a remediation business that helps clients change their balance sheets if they begin to get hiccups in their operating models.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2019 Q1","e":"cfg","d":"2019-04-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"In global markets, FX and interest rate products were up 33% year-over-year led by the IRP team, which was able to win some nice lead transactions and take advantage of the flat yield curve by restructuring the existing client hedges.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2019 Q1","e":"cfg","d":"2019-04-18","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"We are identifying further opportunities to streamline our operations and activities across the organization to capitalize on the next level of efficiencies which include a strong focus on end-to-end automation across the front and back office.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2019 Q1","e":"cfg","d":"2019-04-18","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Bruce Van Saun","x":"So it probably reaffirmed the full-year outlook.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2019 Q1","e":"cfg","d":"2019-04-18","l":"guidance","r":"management","s":"Bruce Van Saun","x":"So that gives us the confidence that broadly reaffirms the outlook, Peter.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2021 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2022-01-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"For example, continuing our multiyear journey of digital transformation across consumer and commercial, looking at further organizational streamlining, accelerating and building on our next gen tech initiatives and doing more in the cloud.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2022 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2023-01-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Don McCree","x":"If you don't get regular way transactions, you're going to get a lot of restructuring transactions.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2022 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2023-01-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Don McCree","x":"So, we're comfortable around where we are with the coverage ratios right now, but we'll be active in restructuring the portfolio.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2023 Q1","e":"cfg","d":"2023-04-19","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Don McCree","x":"We haven’t seen a lot of appraisals yet, because we are not really in the restructuring mode, the ones we have seen have actually been modestly better than we expected.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2023 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2024-01-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"The largest driver was the FDIC special assessment, followed by elevated top and severance related expenses attributable to meaningful headcount reduction.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2023 Q4","e":"cfg","d":"2024-01-17","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"Our reported expense of $1.61 billion increased $319 million, including notable items totaling $323 million, namely the industrywide FDIC special assessment of $225 million, and the impact of taking cost reduction actions to adjust our expense base heading into 2024.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2024 Q3","e":"cfg","d":"2024-10-16","l":"cost_cuts","r":"management","s":"Brendan Coughlin","x":"And now with the federal government not collecting payments again on that portfolio and rates coming back down, we should see more late 20s, early 30 year olds who have great credit coming back in the money that see value in restructuring their student loan debt.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2025 Q1","e":"cfg","d":"2025-04-16","l":"ai_spend","r":"management","s":"Bruce Van Saun","x":"So, things like making sure we're adding to the Private Bank, we're adding private wealth teams, we're opening Private Bank offices, we're investing in AI and various projects, data analytics capability.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2025 Q1","e":"cfg","d":"2025-04-16","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"Bruce Van Saun","x":"The basis for our full year guide had anticipated some choppiness in the first half of the year tied to the rollout of tariffs and downsizing of the federal government.","url":"https://huggingface.co/datasets/kurry/sp500_earnings_transcripts"},{"c":"CFG 2025 Q1","e":"cfg","d":"2025-04-16","l":"tariffs","r":"management","s":"John Woods","x":"Commercial loans were up slightly with a modest increase in line 